====================================================================
PolyKernel T37 Wave 7: NEGATIVE evidence - broken rendezvous is caught
  Break the SUMMA dataflow rendezvous: fire the per-PE compute on the
  A panel ALONE (the compute task is bound to ONLY the x_done color;
  the B broadcast is skipped). The compute then accumulates C_tile +=
  A_panel * (empty B panel) = 0, so the simulator output is WRONG (C
  is all zeros) and FAILS the golden contract C (cosine < 0.999,
  max_rel_err > 1e-2, pcc < 0.99). This proves the dataflow_correctness
  test catches dataflow bugs: a correct rendezvous (compute fires only
  after BOTH the A and B panels arrive) is required for golden-correct
  output.
  (GPU-free functional simulator; no Cerebras hardware involved.)
====================================================================

