The test asserts, for the broken-rendezvous run (compute fires on A alone):
  EXPECT_EQ(res.bWavelets, 0u)        // no B broadcast: compute did not wait for B
  EXPECT_EQ(max|C|, 0.0)              // output is (wrongly) all zeros
  EXPECT_FALSE(contractC.pass)        // FAILS golden contract C
  EXPECT_LT(cosine, 0.999)            // cosine = 0.0
  EXPECT_GT(max_rel_err, 1e-2)        // max_rel_err ~= 1.0
  EXPECT_LT(pcc, 0.99)                // pcc = 0.0
A PASS therefore proves the broken output is wrong AND fails the golden.

